-observations-September-27-2026.html#l:sep:theorem","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":10,"section_title":"Localization by separated tuples","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:16d1fade9ca8099a86cf5b8fffb8afbb87e05e309f59ac935ca3dd5b61550142","file":"preprints/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026/build/sections/drafts/replica-localization/separated-tuples.tex","line":727,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"8fe60c7294cf744e8947b412523a3c1e20e7699219c63cbe42b50c5f3f318597","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026/build/sections/drafts/replica-localization/separated-tuples.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:16d1fade9ca8099a86cf5b8fffb8afbb87e05e309f59ac935ca3dd5b61550142","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026/build/sections/drafts/replica-localization/separated-tuples.tex#L727"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{l:sep:theorem}\nLet \\(M(d)=o(d^2)\\) be integer-valued and let\n\\(0<\\epsilon(d)\\le1/10\\).  Every learner of\nSection~\\ref{l:model} with uniform-sphere angular success probability\nat least \\(2/3\\) must satisfy\n\\[\n T(d)\\ge c\\,d\\log(1/\\epsilon(d))\n\\]\nfor all sufficiently large \\(d\\), with an absolute \\(c>0\\).\nThe eventual dimension threshold may depend on the memory sequence.\nSuccess at least \\(2/3\\) for every fixed signal implies the same\nconclusion by averaging."}
